@page "/accessibility-tree"
<PageTitle>Accessibility tree · Blazor Accessibility Toolkit</PageTitle>

<div class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Browser tests · Playwright</p>
    <h1>Accessibility-tree snapshots</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        A snapshot records what assistive technologies get from a component: roles, accessible names, states and
        hierarchy, without generated ids or styling. You review it once and commit it. When a refactoring changes the
        semantics, the test fails with a readable diff.
    </p>
</div>

<ul class="reasons">
    <li>Stored snapshots live in <code>__a11y_snapshots__</code> next to the test file. A missing snapshot is written and the test fails, so the new file gets reviewed.</li>
    <li>Templates can be partial and can use regular expressions, for example <code>- status: /\d+ results/</code>.</li>
    <li>Run with <code>BLAZOR_A11Y_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1</code> to accept intended changes. On CI, snapshots are never written.</li>
</ul>

<section aria-labelledby="snapshot">
    <h2 id="snapshot">The same template, two implementations</h2>
    <p>
        Both components display the same tabs. The template below was reviewed for the accessible version. The other
        version loses two names: the tablist has none, and the panel is not labelled by its tab.
    </p>
    <ExampleCard Title="Tabs that only work with a mouse" Defect="true" Example="SnapshotExamples.NaiveTabsSnapshot" Sources="@(["NaiveTabs.razor"])">
        <Stage><NaiveTabs Label="Sections" Items="DemoData.Tabs" /></Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
    <ExampleCard Title="Tabs with complete semantics" Example="SnapshotExamples.TabsSnapshot" Sources="@(["Tabs.razor"])">
        <Stage><Tabs Label="Sections" Items="DemoData.Tabs" /></Stage>
    </ExampleCard>
</section>

<div class="callout">
    <p>
        Snapshots catch semantic regressions. They do not prove accessibility: a snapshot of an inaccessible component
        passes too, once it is accepted. Review new snapshots like code.
    </p>
</div>

<p class="next">Next: <a href="ci-gate">turn all of this into a CI gate</a>.</p>
